Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:06:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Speed under load: the short pool to 80; the run trail saved
 in one round trip
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's fourth 200 run (60530) read per run: the prompt's own reads
queued ~7.6 s (1 s alone), a contact search 6.4 s (2.2 s alone), and the
post-run 5–7 s (2 s alone) — all waiting on database connections, the model
itself unchanged at ~19 s. The short pool goes 40 → 80 (the database allows
2,091). The run's trail, written one row per round trip before the owner saw
the answer, is now one statement with the order kept a microsecond apart.

